From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martijn Muijsers <martijnmuijsers@live.nl>
Date: Sat, 26 Nov 2022 11:25:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Leaf: Reduce array allocations

Ported to Luminol from Leaf (https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf/blob/ver/26.2/leaf-server/minecraft-patches/features/0042-Reduce-array-allocations.patch)
Original license: GPL-3.0-only (https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf/blob/ver/26.2/LICENSE.md)
Gale - https://galemc.org

This is the follow-up delta on top of the already-applied Gale patch
(0081-Gale-Reduce-array-allocations): ServerLevel#getCurrentlyTickingEntities
and the remaining EquipmentSlot iteration sites in Mob.
Leaf's PurpurCommand hunk is dropped because PurpurCommand does not
exist in the Folia/Luminol source tree.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
index 7016a277ecf594682b9c1bb6c12009b67cc959e6..be6a0fa5ccbaa7a3af6ba0c70f16409436ac9ba0 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
@@ -1462,7 +1462,7 @@ public class ServerLevel extends Level implements WorldGenLevel, ServerEntityGet
 
     public static List<Entity> getCurrentlyTickingEntities() {
         Entity ticking = currentlyTickingEntity.get();
-        List<Entity> ret = java.util.Arrays.asList(ticking == null ? new Entity[0] : new Entity[] { ticking });
+        List<Entity> ret = java.util.Arrays.asList(ticking == null ? me.titaniumtown.ArrayConstants.emptyEntityArray : new Entity[] { ticking }); // Gale - JettPack - reduce array allocations
 
         return ret;
     }
